.TH MONIKER 1 "September 2026" "moniker 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
moniker \- reserve a friendly, unique team name
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B moniker -dir
.I ABS_REGISTRY
.RB [ -theme " playful|space|nature" ]
.RB [ -json ]
.br
.B moniker mcp -dir
.I ABS_REGISTRY
.B tools/call
.br
.B moniker version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reserve one friendly team name in an explicitly selected private directory.
There is no model, network, ambient configuration or daemon.
Themes are playful (default), space and nature.
.PP
The registry must be absolute. Missing directories are created with mode 0700.
An existing registry must have mode 0700 and must not be a symlink.
Reservations are mode 0600 JSON files named after generated slugs. Atomic
exclusive creation prevents duplicate names among concurrent processes and
later invocations using the same intact registry.
.PP
After 32 dictionary collisions, try up to 16 randomly suffixed names. Names
are never automatically released. An interrupted response can leave a name
occupied; retrying creates a different reservation.
.SH OUTPUT
Plain stdout contains one display name and a newline.
.B -json
prints id (32 lowercase hexadecimal characters), name, slug (lowercase ASCII
words separated by hyphens), and theme. Diagnostics go to stderr.
.SH MCP DISPATCHER
Use mcp/manifest.json with the separate mcpserve and dispatcher argv
.BR "moniker mcp -dir ABS_REGISTRY" .
tools/call implements generate_team_name with an optional theme argument.
Parameters are one UTF-8 JSON object of at most 4096 bytes. Unknown fields,
duplicates, invalid types and trailing data are rejected. Arguments cannot
change the registry. Results contain content and structuredContent. Tool
errors set isError and exit zero. Unknown methods return error -32601 and
exit one. Calls are local writes and are not idempotent.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0: name reserved or MCP result returned.
.br
1: runtime or unsupported dispatcher method failure.
.br
2: invalid invocation.
.SH FILES
.I ABS_REGISTRY/SLUG.json
is the durable reservation. Deleting or changing records voids the corresponding
uniqueness guarantee. There is no default registry location.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mcpserve (1)
